# 52. TEN-STAR DEFINITION OF DONE

A result is complete when:

### 1. PURPOSE

It solves the intended human problem.

### 2. SOURCE

The correct source was inspected.

### 3. PRESERVATION

Known-good functionality remains intact.

### 4. ARCHITECTURE

The correct layer was changed.

### 5. QUALITY

The result is premium.

### 6. ACCESSIBILITY

The intended users can use it.

### 7. BUILD

The artifact actually builds.

### 8. RUNTIME

The intended runtime is independently observed.

### 9. INTELLIGENCE

Reusable learning is captured.

### 10. CONTINUITY

The next Naya can continue intelligently.

